  {
   "id": "E1",
   "kind": "execution after the evidence clock keeps its onset",
   "claim": "With no execution, and with execution after the evidence clock T* (at 12 h, by commitment or by the cue fading; at 6 h only before it), a signal half of T* or T* after a 4 x 4 memory damage (3.3 or 6.5 h) repairs no more than 0.02 below a prompt one at equal elapsed time, on average",
   "rule": "HOLDS if on average over the twelve unit-body pairs, dial-c's r_in in memory4@0 at t = 4,000 exceeds its r_in in memory4@round(m T*) at t = round(m T*) + 4,000 by at most 0.02, for clocks SL, C12 and F12 at m = 0.5 and 1 and for C6 at m = 0.5, else FAILS",
   "thresholds": {
    "loss": 0.02
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "E2",
   "kind": "after execution a late signal is worth almost nothing",
   "claim": "A signal that arrives after the tissue has executed its default outcome (commitment at 6, 12 or 24 h, or the cue fading at 12 h) repairs a 4 x 4 memory damage at most 0.05 more than no signal at the same time, on average",
   "rule": "HOLDS if on average over the twelve unit-body pairs, dial-c's r_in in memory4@D at D + 4,000 exceeds never-c's r_in in memory4@0 at the same read by at most 0.05, for C6 at m = 1, 2 and 4, C12 at m = 2 and 4, C24 at m = 4 and F12 at m = 2 and 4 (D = round(m T*)), else FAILS",
   "thresholds": {
    "worth": 0.05
   }
  },
  {
   "id": "E3",
   "kind": "the window closes when the tissue executes",
   "claim": "At each delay of 1, 2 and 4 T* (6.5, 13.1 and 26.1 h), a late signal is worth at least 0.2 more over no signal in a tissue that has not yet executed than in one that has just executed (commitment at 6, 12 and 24 h), paired within each case, on average",
   "rule": "HOLDS if on average over the twelve unit-body pairs, gain(C12, 1) - gain(C6, 1), gain(C24, 2) - gain(C12, 2) and gain(SL, 4) - gain(C24, 4) are each >= 0.2, where gain(c, m) is dial-c's r_in in memory4@round(m T*) at round(m T*) + 4,000 less never-c's r_in in memory4@0 at the same read, else FAILS",
   "thresholds": {
    "drop": 0.2
   }
  },
